From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ken Smith <ken@design-nex.us>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 13:40:45 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] fullscreen: misc:fullscreen_own_workspace

A window that goes truly fullscreen (not maximized) moves to a workspace
of its own, named fullscreen-<origin>-<n>, that sits right after the
workspace it came from: a fullscreen started on 2 is between 2 and 3 for
m+1/m-1, workspace swipes (with or without workspace_swipe_wrap) and the
slide animation. Leaving fullscreen moves it back and shows its
workspace, recreating it if the window was its only one; closing it
returns there too, and the fullscreen workspace goes away. Several
fullscreen windows from one workspace follow it in the order they went
fullscreen.

The change is handled once it settles, as moves, floating changes and
group swaps turn fullscreen off and straight back on. Windows on special
workspaces, pinned or being dragged, already on a fullscreen workspace,
moved elsewhere while fullscreen, or tagged fullscreen-in-place stay
where they are. A new window from another app that opens on a
fullscreen workspace goes to the workspace it came from; the app's own
dialogs stay.

r+N/r-N still count by ID: they step over fullscreen workspaces, and
from one count from the workspace it came from. State lives in the new
Fullscreen::spaces() manager, so no existing class changes layout.
